course: dictionary
lesson: 1453
title: Cash and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word cash has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one is meant. «Theo's grandma sent twenty pounds in cash, and Theo announced it was all going on games.» Here cash means money in coins and notes, not money on a card. The words twenty pounds and in cash give the clue.
explain: Cash can also mean money in general. In «cash flow problem», the phrase is about having no money to pay the bills, not about coins or notes. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then swap your meaning in and check it still makes sense.
explain: Cash can also be a verb, which is an action word. To cash a cheque is to change it into money. The endings cashes, cashed and cashing show it is being used as an action, so you can spot the verb by how the word is used.
fact: Cash means money in coins and notes, not money on a card.
fact: «Cash» can also mean money in general, as in «cash flow problem», which often means having no money to pay the bills.
fact: To cash a cheque means to change it into money.
fact: A cash machine, or ATM, reads the card's chip, checks the PIN with the bank and counts out notes.
fact: The first cash machine opened in London in 1967.
exercise: «Theo's grandma sent twenty pounds in cash.» What does cash mean here? | A bank in London | Coins and notes | A card with a chip | * Coins and notes, not money on a card
exercise: «Cash flow problem» often means what? | * Having no money to pay the bills | Having too many coins in a jar | Paying with a cheque | Losing a card
exercise: To cash a cheque means to | Lend it to a friend | * Change it into money | Tear it up and post it
test: «A cash machine reads the card's chip and counts out notes.» What does a cash machine count out? | Cheques | * Notes | Pebbles | Books
test: Tom kept a pile of cash in his schoolbag to show off. What went wrong? | Nothing went wrong | * It was stolen at break | It was sent home by post
exam: Which phrase uses cash to mean money in general? | To cash a cheque is to change it into money | A cash machine counts out notes | * Cash flow problem means having no money to pay the bills | Pay in cash at the till
